    "narrative": "For our August 8th slate, **Seiya Suzuki** (67.36) and **Corbin Carroll** (64.88) headline our offensive output. **Seiya Suzuki** is the premier play of the day, benefiting from a favorable 4.66 xERA matchup against Seth Lugo and an elite #2 spot in the order, which yields an 8% boost. While **Corbin Carroll** faces a tougher test against Yoshinobu Yamamoto, his profile remains elite due to a significant platoon advantage and the aggressive base-running upside required to chase our stolen base scarcity targets. Similarly, **Isaac Paredes** (64.27) and **Brice Turang** (64.10) are locked into strong starts, with **Brice Turang** receiving a specific bump for his matchup against Taj Bradley, where his speed profile is well-positioned to capitalize on a favorable stolen base environment.\n\nPlatoon edges are the primary catalyst for our roster construction today. **Isaac Paredes** earns a massive 9% boost from his dynamic platoon split, effectively counteracting a neutral park factor. While **Jose Caballero** faces a steep challenge in Chris Sale, his 13% platoon boost and favorable wind conditions keep his efficiency at a solid 55.28, justifying the start despite the high-tier opposing arm. Conversely, we are keeping **Zach McKinstry** on the bench with a 42.34 score; while he benefits from wind-aided hitting conditions, his marginal projection is weighed down by an inefficient #9 order slot and a difficult defensive matchup, ultimately pushing him just outside our starting threshold.\n\nRisk mitigation remains a priority as we navigate a lineup-pending environment. Most of our starters are carrying \"Lineup Pending\" designations, requiring last-minute verification before first pitch to ensure we do not lose efficiency in the #1\u2013#4 slots. Furthermore, while **Gabriel Moreno** and **Austin Riley** are starting, they face the high-level arms of Yoshinobu Yamamoto and Gerrit Cole, respectively; we are banking on their high-percentage recency and favorable park/wind factors to carry them through these tough matchups. With **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** confirmed as unavailable due to IL designations, our depth is thinner than usual, placing a premium on the performance of our primary starters to maintain our Roto standings.",
